<section class="science-hero">
  <div class="science-hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">THE LIVING SCIENCE OF FRUIT</span><h1>From blossom<br><em>to flavour.</em></h1><p>Fruit is a living plant structure and a remarkable food chemistry system. Follow how cells grow, flowers are pollinated, pigments form, aromas emerge and texture changes as fruit ripens.</p><div class="science-hero-actions"><a href="#chemistry" class="button-primary">Explore chemistry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="#biology" class="light-link">Explore biology <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
  <div class="science-hero-photo"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559181567-c3190ca9959b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1100&h=1100&q=88" alt="Fresh red cherries showing the natural colour and texture of ripe fruit" fetchpriority="high"><div class="science-photo-caption">A closer look at living food</div></div>
</section>
<section class="section-block science-intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">A BRIDGE BETWEEN DISCIPLINES</span><h2>One fruit, many sciences.</h2></div><p>Botany explains where a fruit comes from. Cell biology describes its living tissues. Chemistry helps explain sweetness, acidity, colour and aroma. Ecology shows how fruits and seeds interact with wildlife, habitats and people. These perspectives connect to each other, but each answers a different question.</p></section>
<section class="science-track" id="chemistry"><div class="science-track-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523049673857-eb18f1d7b578?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=85" alt="A freshly cut avocado showing green flesh and the texture of its edible tissue" loading="lazy"></div><div class="science-track-content"><span class="eyebrow">FOOD CHEMISTRY</span><h2>The molecules behind the experience.</h2><p>Sugars and organic acids shape taste. Pigments create colour. Volatile compounds carry aroma. Pectin and cell-wall chemistry influence texture and the way fruit behaves in cooking.</p><div class="science-guide-list"><% chemistryGuides.forEach(function(guide) { %><a href="/guide/<%= guide.slug %>"><span><%= guide.title %></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><% }); %></div></div></section>
<section class="science-track science-track-reverse" id="biology"><div class="science-track-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1455659817273-f96807779a8a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=85" alt="Delicate spring blossoms representing the flowering stage of fruit development" loading="lazy"></div><div class="science-track-content"><span class="eyebrow">PLANT BIOLOGY</span><h2>The living process behind the harvest.</h2><p>Flowers, pollen, ovules, cells and plant hormones coordinate fruit development. Seeds are protected and dispersed in many ways, while water movement and tissue structure influence growth, firmness and freshness.</p><div class="science-guide-list"><% biologyGuides.forEach(function(guide) { %><a href="/guide/<%= guide.slug %>"><span><%= guide.title %></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><% }); %></div></div></section>
<section class="science-field-note"><div class="science-field-note-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523712999610-f77fbcfc3843?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=85" alt="Sunlight filtering through a dense forest canopy and a living ecosystem" loading="lazy"></div><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">BEYOND THE LAB</span><h2>Fruit belongs to a living landscape.</h2><p>Pollinators, soil life, weather, water and habitat all affect fruit-bearing plants. Learning the biology of a fruit is also a way to understand the landscapes, farms and communities connected to it.</p><a href="/guides?category=Ecology%20%26%20sustainability" class="light-link">Read about ecology & sustainability ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section-block"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">KEEP EXPLORING</span><h2>Take the science into the fruit atlas.</h2><p>Move from the underlying biology and chemistry to individual fruit profiles, growing advice and careful food handling.</p></div></div><div class="quick-link-grid"><a href="/fruits"><strong>Browse fruit profiles</strong><span>Explore names, structure, flavour and origin.</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="/growing"><strong>Growing & horticulture</strong><span>Connect plant biology with the growing environment.</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="/storage"><strong>Ripening & storage</strong><span>Understand freshness, texture and careful handling.</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="/glossary"><strong>Science glossary</strong><span>Build a vocabulary for botanical and food science.</span><b>↗</b></a></div></section>
